{
 "section_summary": "This section continues a confidential economic survey of Japan, evaluating the country’s dependence on foreign supplies of animal products, fibers, chemicals, fertilizers, timber, petroleum, and strategic metals, with particular attention to the likely effectiveness of embargoes. It then examines mining, heavy industry, manufacturing, electric power, and foreign trade, emphasizing the requirements of Japan’s war economy and its continuing dependence on the United States, the British Empire, and Southeast Asia. The final pages survey Japan’s strained rail, road, and maritime transportation systems and merchant fleet.",
