   "about": "A strategic survey assesses Japan's material resources, industrial capacity, foreign trade, and transportation, emphasizing vulnerabilities to coordinated embargoes.",
   "summary": "The report continues its commodity-by-commodity assessment with hides, wool, asbestos, jute, rubber, silk, cotton, oils, chemicals, fertilizers, timber, and other materials, frequently comparing Japanese requirements with foreign sources of supply. It then analyzes petroleum, coal, iron and steel, aluminum, copper, nickel, and other strategic minerals, identifying imports whose interruption could constrain military production. Later sections describe wartime changes in manufacturing, electric-power shortages, machinery and munitions production, and Japan's shifting trade toward the Yen Bloc while remaining dependent on free-exchange countries. The concluding pages describe overburdened railways, fuel-starved road transport, shipbuilding, the merchant marine, dockyards, ports, and changing Asian trade routes.",
